                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Expanding upon the first game, this one has bigger and more complex levels, with a greater variety of environments, while retaining the focus on exploration and puzzles that made the first game good. However, it doesn't do much to improve upon the core gameplay, which remains mostly unchanged. The environments are more varied and generally still interesting, but they often lack the atmosphere of the first game. There's less of a feeling of isolation and exploring long-forgotten places, something that's further diminished by the greater number of human enemies you encounter throughout.",
